## **What is the NRA CCW Advanced Pistol Course?**

The NRA CCW Advanced Pistol Course at Live Fire Instruction is an intensive training program focused on developing a defensive mindset and advanced handgun skills. Located at the NRA Range in **Fairfax, Virginia**, this course is designed for experienced shooters who already possess a basic understanding of pistol operation and wish to carry a concealed firearm ethically and responsibly.

The curriculum moves beyond basic marksmanship to cover tactical techniques such as drawing from a holster, reloading under stress, and clearing common firearm stoppages. Special emphasis is placed on situational awareness, mental preparedness, and the principles of effective concealment in real-world scenarios. Students must provide their own firearm, holster, and concealment garment to participate in the live-fire drills. Led by NRA-certified instructors, this course provides the knowledge and confidence necessary for permit holders to carry a handgun safely in public while adhering to Virginia's legal requirements for self-defense and responsible ownership.

---

## **Advanced Concealed Carry Training Topics**

This course is structured around a full-day curriculum blending classroom instruction with supervised live-fire drills. Below is an overview of the core topics covered during your training session:

### Defensive Mindset & Threat Avoidance

Understanding the psychology of self-defense is the foundation of responsible concealed carry. Students will explore legal, ethical, and situational frameworks for deciding when and how to use a firearm in a defensive encounter — and more importantly, how to avoid confrontation altogether through awareness and de-escalation.

### Drawing from a Holster

Participants will learn and practice a safe, repeatable draw stroke from a dominant-side hip holster. Drills emphasize proper grip acquisition, trigger discipline during the draw, and consistent muzzle presentation — all essential skills for any concealed carry permit holder.

### Recoil Management & Follow-Up Shots

Effective defensive shooting requires controlled recoil. Students train with proper stance (Weaver or isosceles), grip pressure, and follow-through technique to place rapid, accurate follow-up shots on target.

### Reloading Under Stress & Malfunction Clearing

Live-fire drills cover emergency reloads, tactical reloads, and clearing Type 1 (failure to fire), Type 2 (stovepipe), and Type 3 (double feed) malfunctions — all under realistic time constraints.

---

## **Prerequisites & Gear Requirements**

### Who Is This Course For?

This is an **intermediate-to-advanced level** course. It is ideal for:

- Virginia Concealed Handgun Permit (CHP) holders seeking tactical skill development
- Shooters who have completed a basic pistol course and are ready to advance
- Active carry permit holders looking to build confidence drawing from a holster
- Competitive or recreational shooters expanding their defensive skillset

*Prior pistol experience is required. This course is not suitable for first-time or beginner shooters.*

### Required Gear Checklist

- Personally-owned handgun (semi-automatic recommended)
- Dominant-side hip holster (no cross-draw, shoulder, or appendix holsters)
- Sturdy belt designed for holster carry
- Two magazines + magazine pouch
- Suitable concealment garment (jacket, vest, or cover shirt)
- Billed cap (safety requirement on the range)
- 125 rounds of ammunition (available for purchase at the NRA Range pro shop)
- Lunch (full-day course with classroom and range sessions)

---

## **Course Location & NRA Range Details**

This course is held exclusively at the **NRA Headquarters Range**, one of the premier indoor shooting facilities in the Washington D.C. metropolitan area.

**NRA Range — 11250 Waples Mill Rd, Fairfax, VA 22030**

Live Fire Instruction serves students throughout Northern Virginia including Fairfax County, Loudoun County, Prince William County, Arlington, and Alexandria.

