## **Frequently Asked Questions**

#### **What gear do I need to bring to the NRA CCW Advanced Pistol Course?**

You must bring your own personally-owned firearm, a dominant-side hip holster, a sturdy carry belt, two magazines, a mag pouch, a suitable concealment garment (such as a jacket or vest), a billed cap, and lunch. You will also need 125 rounds of ammunition, which can be purchased directly at the NRA Range pro shop on the day of class.

#### **Does this course satisfy Virginia concealed carry permit requirements?**

This is an advanced skills course designed for shooters who already hold or are pursuing a Virginia Concealed Handgun Permit (CHP). It is not a standalone course for the initial permit application, but it significantly enhances the defensive competency of current permit holders. Contact us if you need guidance on which course is right for your permit or training goals.

#### **Are ammo and range fees included in the $165 course price?**

No. The $165.00 course fee covers classroom instruction and range supervision by NRA-certified instructors. Range lane fees ($15–$35) and ammunition (125 rounds required) are separate costs paid directly to the NRA Range on the day of your class. Ammunition is available for purchase on-site at the NRA Range pro shop.

#### **Do I need prior shooting experience to enroll?**

Yes. This is an intermediate-to-advanced level course. Students must already be comfortable handling, loading, and safely operating a semi-automatic pistol. If you are new to shooting, we recommend starting with the [NRA Basic Pistol Course](/nra-basic-pistol-course-fairfax-va) or [First Step Pistol Orientation](/first-step-pistol-orientation-fairfax-va) before attending this advanced class.

#### **What is the refund or cancellation policy?**

Please contact us directly at [class@livefireinstruction.com](mailto:class@livefireinstruction.com) or call [1-571-210-5651](tel:15712105651) to discuss scheduling changes or cancellations prior to your course date.

